<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading"><a class="h" href="https://gerrit.googlesource.com/gerrit/+/refs/heads/master#Build"></a><a class="h" href="https://gerrit.googlesource.com/gerrit/+/refs/heads/master#build"></a>Build</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Install&nbsp;<a href="https://bazel.build/versions/master/docs/install.html">Bazel</a>&nbsp;and run the following:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:preformatted -->
<pre class="wp-block-preformatted">    git clone --recurse-submodules https://gerrit.googlesource.com/gerrit
    cd gerrit &amp;&amp; bazel build release
</pre>
<!-- /wp:preformatted -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading"><a class="h" href="https://gerrit.googlesource.com/gerrit/+/refs/heads/master#Install-binary-packages-Deb_Rpm"></a><a class="h" href="https://gerrit.googlesource.com/gerrit/+/refs/heads/master#install-binary-packages-deb_rpm"></a>Install binary packages (Deb/Rpm)</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The instruction how to configure GerritForge/BinTray repositories is&nbsp;<a href="https://gitenterprise.me/2015/02/27/gerrit-2-10-rpm-and-debian-packages-available/">here</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>On Debian/Ubuntu run:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:preformatted -->
<pre class="wp-block-preformatted">    apt-get update &amp;&amp; apt-get install gerrit=&lt;version&gt;-&lt;release&gt;
</pre>
<!-- /wp:preformatted -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><em>NOTE: release is a counter that starts with 1 and indicates the number of packages that have been released with the same version of the software.</em></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>On CentOS/RedHat run:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:preformatted -->
<pre class="wp-block-preformatted">    yum clean all &amp;&amp; yum install gerrit-&lt;version&gt;[-&lt;release&gt;]
</pre>
<!-- /wp:preformatted -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>On Fedora run:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:preformatted -->
<pre class="wp-block-preformatted">    dnf clean all &amp;&amp; dnf install gerrit-&lt;version&gt;[-&lt;release&gt;]
</pre>
<!-- /wp:preformatted -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading"><a class="h" href="https://gerrit.googlesource.com/gerrit/+/refs/heads/master#Use-pre_built-Gerrit-images-on-Docker"></a><a class="h" href="https://gerrit.googlesource.com/gerrit/+/refs/heads/master#use-pre_built-gerrit-images-on-docker"></a>Use pre-built Gerrit images on Docker</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Docker images of Gerrit are available on&nbsp;<a href="https://hub.docker.com/u/gerritforge/">DockerHub</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>To run a CentOS 8 based Gerrit image:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:preformatted -->
<pre class="wp-block-preformatted">    docker run -p 8080:8080 gerritcodereview/gerrit[:version]-centos8
</pre>
<!-- /wp:preformatted -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>To run a Ubuntu 20.04 based Gerrit image:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:preformatted -->
<pre class="wp-block-preformatted">    docker run -p 8080:8080 gerritcodereview/gerrit[:version]-ubuntu20
</pre>
<!-- /wp:preformatted -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><em>NOTE: release is optional. Last released package of the version is installed if the release number is omitted.</em></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

